# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 15-privacy-incident-override

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

ANALYTICS AND THIRD-PARTY DATA COLLECTION
(APP-PRIVACY-\*) — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-PRIVACY-NO-AD-ID [GATE]

\- Do not use advertising identifiers, fingerprinting,
session replay, or behavioral profiling in N78

  applications
unless a product-specific policy explicitly permits it.



APP-PRIVACY-THIRD-PARTY-SDK [GATE]

\- Third-party SDKs that collect, transmit, or analyze
user or device data require explicit review

  before
inclusion.



APP-PRIVACY-ANALYTICS-CONSENT [QA]

\- If optional analytics are ever introduced, the
collection purpose, data collected, destination,

  retention, and
user choice must be explicitly documented.





\================================================================================

VULNERABILITY AND INCIDENT RESPONSE
(APP-SEC-RESPONSE-\*) — FAMILY

\================================================================================



APP-SEC-VULNERABILITY-RESPONSE [QA]

\- Maintain a documented process for receiving,
assessing, prioritizing, fixing, and communicating

  material
security vulnerabilities affecting released products.



APP-SEC-CRITICAL-FIX [QA]

\- Material vulnerabilities affecting released products
must receive an explicit severity, owner,

  remediation
decision, and target action.



APP-SEC-RELEASE-RECALL [QA]

\- The product family must have a documented response
path for a release that must be withdrawn,

  replaced, or
urgently patched.





\================================================================================

OVERRIDE GOVERNANCE (APP-OVERRIDE-\*) — EVERY PRODUCT

\================================================================================



(Complements STANDARD OVERRIDES — ACCEPTED DEVIATIONS
PER PRODUCT above; does not replace it.)



APP-OVERRIDE-OWNER [QA]

\- Every active override must identify the product,
rule ID, reason, approving owner, date approved,

  and
compensating control where applicable.



APP-OVERRIDE-REVIEW [QA]

\- Every active override must have a defined review
date or review trigger.

\- Overrides must not become permanent merely because
they were once approved.



APP-OVERRIDE-RISK [QA]

\- Overrides that weaken security, privacy, data
integrity, or release controls must identify the

  associated
risk and why the exception is acceptable.



APP-OVERRIDE-CLEANUP [QA]

\- When a product no longer requires an override, the
override must be revoked and the affected

  standard rule
restored.





\================================================================================

